WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.968
The world's second largest

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:06.539
economy had a tough year in 2023.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.408
Now one of Beijing's answers

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.542
to the challenge

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.379
ban and erase criticism of it.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:12.979
In December,

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.280
China's Ministry of State

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.584
Security issued this order resolutely

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.185
crack down and punish

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.887
illegal criminal activities

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:21.721
that endanger

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.023
national security

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.692
in the economic security field.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.128
Apparently, that includes disappearing

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.295
negative commentary

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:30.997
from the already heavily

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.732
censored Chinese Internet.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.034
So is she even bothered

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.835
to read those orders on December 1st?

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.270
This prominent economic

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.938
professor, Yuji Ping,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.006
advised people

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.941
not to invest in the falling

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.777
Chinese stock market.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.312
Now, all of Professor Liu's social media

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.947
accounts are frozen

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.416
and when you click to follow him,

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:50.350
you get this message,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.651
which translates

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:54.654
It is forbidden to follow this user

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:58.058
due to their violation of relevant rules.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:00:58.958
CNN found

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.928
similar freezes temporarily imposed on

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.630
at least five other Chinese

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.698
economic analysts

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.734
also removed from the Internet.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.670
Saw this documentary highlighting

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.905
economic hardship

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:14.441
among Chinese migrant workers.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.809
I think the Chinese economy

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.812
is at a cliff edge at the moment.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:19.712
I don't think

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.715
it has not fallen off the cliff yet,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.017
but it's getting to a point

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:27.787
where things can get much more difficult.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:28.555
Officially,

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.889
the Chinese economy grew

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.358
by more than 5% last year,

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.960
but the country's youth unemployment

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.963
rate keeps hitting record highs.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.098
Then there's China's

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:38.898
all important

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.200
real estate sector,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.036
which along with related industries, used

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:46.506
to make up 30% of the Chinese economy.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.108
This is the Hong Kong office

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.210
of the biggest symbol of China's

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.312
real estate crisis, Evergrande.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.546
Until two years ago,

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.581
this company

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:57.383
was the largest homebuilder in China,

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.053
employing some 200,000 people.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.655
Then the company defaulted on its debt

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:03.990
and now a court here in Hong

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.459
Kong has ordered the liquidation

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:10.730
of Evergrande.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.364
Across the

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.367
country, protests as angry new homebuyers

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.270
demand completion of unfinished homes

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.740
that they've already paid for.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.343
Perhaps the only other sector gloomier

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.111
is the country's stock market.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.546
In the past three years,

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.247
the combined

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.481
Chinese stock market

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.484
lost more than $6 trillion.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.418
To show you me,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.753
I haven't made any money

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.988
out of the stock market,

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.757
so I sold all my stocks.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:38.491
If you don't sell,

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.259
I hope

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.960
the Chinese economy is strong

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.495
and it will be stronger,

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.697
says this Beijing resident.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.232
Perhaps she got the message

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.934
from this recent meeting of the country's

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.736
top propaganda officials.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.870
Their order

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.873
amplify bright prospects of the economy.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.609
As China heads into 2024.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.810
All you know

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.045
so before I bring Ivan in,

00:02:59.045 --> 00:02:59.946
I want to show you

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.148
CNN's feed of this program

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.150
as it's being seen in China

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.418
or more accurately,

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.021
at what Chinese censors replaced it with.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.390
As soon as we mentioned the story

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.325
that you just saw again.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.661
Color bars there, it's not going out.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.161
So, Ivan,

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.096
if China is censoring economists

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.898
and CNN's reporting about it

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.066
and most of their economic

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.601
data is released,

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.403
it comes from the Chinese government.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.637
How hard is it to get a true picture

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.340
of the state of the Chinese economy?

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.708
Well, it's a big question.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.042
It's long

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.143
been a big question

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:33.313
for economists and investors.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.182
The reliability of these numbers,

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.884
especially back in August

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.219
when the government announced

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.287
it would stop publishing youth

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.455
unemployment numbers

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:45.658
after several months of record highs,

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.327
the mood has changed a lot.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.361
You know, foreign companies,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.495
they used to line up to try

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.031
to get access to the huge Chinese market.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.166
Last year, for the first time

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.001
in 25 years, John.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.437
Foreign direct investment into China

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:58.638
went into the negative.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:03:59.939
That means foreign companies

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.941
appeared to be pulling out more money

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.142
than they were investing

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:04.677
into their corporations,

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:05.645
into their operations.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.879
Companies like Vanguard

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.382
that asset management company telling CNN

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.717
it was selling its stake

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:13.152
and closing its office in Shanghai

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.954
at the end of last year.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:15.989
So the Chinese government,

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:16.856
it's got a long way

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.891
to go to rebuild its credibility

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.927
with international corporations

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.328
and also, I'd argue,

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.564
with ordinary Chinese consumers.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:27.533
And I'm not sure that censorship

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.068
and ordering officials

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:31.838
to paint rosy pictures about the economy,

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.706
that that's a winning strategy

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.508
to build consumer confidence

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:36.676
in an economy

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.678
that clearly has some big problems.

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.046
Ivan, revealing report there.

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.147
Thank you very much.

